s6-3-p4 = prose (cons "One can now define a transformation on the *interpreter*, not just on its input programs. For example, the interpreter can be transformed into an interpreter returning both a value and an expression witnessing its symbolic dependence on the input, or into an evaluator over a different semiring. To make the latter exact, replace the natural-number carrier by a semiring \(R\) and interpret `num(n)` using the canonical homomorphism \(\mathbb N\to R\). The same syntax then admits a family of interpretations:" nil)
